Katana ZERO DLC still coming, now &#8220;the size of a full sequel&#8221;
Tthe long-awaited Katana ZERO downloadable content, which was previously announced to be free, is still coming and has grown to &#8220;the zei of a full sequel,&#8221; developer Askiisoft announced.
&#8220;I&#8217;m still working hard on the Katana ZERO [downloadable content],&#8221; Askiisoft said in a tweet . &#8220;We made it bigger. It&#8217;s the size of a full sequel, plus a soundtrack of over 30+ new songs. More updates to come. Thanks for your continued support!&#8221;
Katana ZERO is available now for Xbox One , Switch , and PC via Steam , GOG , and Humble Store . A PlayStation 4 version was rated by the Entertainment Software Rating Board back in March 2021.
It is unclear whether the downloadable content is still planned to be free when it launches.
